---
import { BOOK_CALL_HREF } from '../lib/cta';

const FAQ = [
	{
		q: 'Do I need to know anything about tech?',
		a: 'No. You tell us how your business works today, in your own words. We handle everything technical and explain choices in plain language.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What does a6n actually build?',
		a: 'The software your business runs on: a website your customers use, an app for them on their phone, and one screen where you and your staff run orders, bookings, payments and messages.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Why is it called a6n?',
		a: 'It stands for (Ai)ny Management System: one system that can run any kind of business, built for yours.',
	},
	{
		q: 'How long does it take?',
		a: "It depends on what you need. Because we start from parts already running for other businesses, a first version comes together much faster than building from zero. We'll give you a clear plan after the first call.",
	},
	{
		q: 'How much does it cost?',
		a: 'Every business is different, so we quote after a short call, once we understand what you need.',
	},
	{
		q: 'I already use spreadsheets or another system. Can you move it over?',
		a: 'Yes. We bring your customers and records across, so you start in the new app without losing anything.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Can my customers pay online?',
		a: 'Yes. Our clients take card payments, bank transfers, UPI and cash, depending on the country and what suits the business.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Can I send messages to my customers?',
		a: 'Yes. Order emails, reminders and offers go out automatically, with in-app notices too. If a message fails, it is sent again.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What happens if something breaks?',
		a: 'We keep watch every day and fix it. We work like your own tech team, so you talk to the same people who built it.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Where are you based?',
		a: 'We work mainly from Singapore and India, and we build for businesses anywhere. Our clients today are in Canada, Singapore and India.',
	},
];
---

<section class="faq" id="faq">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h2 data-split="lines">Things owners ask us.</h2>
		<div class="list">
			{
				FAQ.map((item, i) => (
					<details>
						<summary>
							<span class="q">{item.q}</span>
							<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true" />
						</summary>
						<p>{item.a}</p>
					</details>
				))
			}
		</div>
		<p class="more">
			Something else? <a href={BOOK_CALL_HREF}>Ask us on a call.</a>
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.faq {
		padding-block: 88px;
	}
	h2 {
		margin-top: 12px;
		font-size: var(--t-xl);
		line-height: 0.92;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
	}
	.list {
		margin-top: 36px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--faint);
	}
	details {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint);
	}
	summary {
		list-style: none;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 24px;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 12px;
		min-height: 44px;
		padding: 20px 0;
		cursor: pointer;
		color: var(--strong);
		font: 500 clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem) / 1.3 var(--font-body);
	}
	summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}
	.q {
		transition: translate 500ms var(--ease);
	}
	@media (hover: hover) {
		summary:hover .q {
			translate: 10px 0;
		}
		summary:hover .plus {
			rotate: 90deg;
		}
	}
	summary:focus-visible .q {
		translate: 10px 0;
	}
	.plus {
		transition: rotate 500ms var(--ease);
	}
	.plus {
		position: relative;
		width: 14px;
		height: 14px;
		align-self: center;
	}
	.plus::before,
	.plus::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		inset: 6px 0 auto;
		height: 2px;
		background: var(--sanguine);
		transition: transform 200ms var(--ease);
	}
	.plus::after {
		transform: rotate(90deg);
	}
	details[open] .plus::after {
		transform: rotate(0deg);
	}
	details p {
		max-width: 64ch;
		padding: 0 0 22px;
	}
	.more {
		margin-top: 24px;
	}
	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.faq {
			padding-block: 56px;
		}
		details p {
			padding-left: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
